  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFirst slice of the self-hosted PR review agent from #1: the **trigger\r\npipeline** and the **outbound-only GitHub poller**. Nothing here spends\r\ntokens or posts to GitHub \u2014 the spending rails land before anything can\r\nspend, per the phase ordering in #1.\r\n\r\n25 files, +1836. Two commits: the initial scaffold, and a follow-up\r\naddressing the first review round (rate-limit hardening, decision logging).\r\n\r\n## What's in\r\n\r\n### Trigger classifier \u2014 `src/pr_review_agent/triggers/`\r\n\r\nExactly two events start a review:\r\n\r\n1. a freshly opened PR whose **author** is allowlisted;\r\n2. a comment containing `@claude` whose **commenter** is allowlisted.\r\n\r\nGating the mention on the commenter is what lets a maintainer summon a\r\nreview of an outside contribution that would not be auto-reviewed.\r\n\r\n| Rejected event | Reason code |\r\n| :-- | :-- |\r\n| Push to an existing PR | never classified \u2014 the poller emits no push event |\r\n| Draft PR | `draft` |\r\n| PR from an unlisted author | `author_not_allowlisted` |\r\n| Comment from an unlisted account | `commenter_not_allowlisted` |\r\n| Any bot, including the agent itself | `bot_author` / `bot_commenter` |\r\n| `@claude` in a fence, code span or blockquote | `no_mention` |\r\n| Already-open PR seen on first poll | `not_fresh` |\r\n\r\nTwo decisions worth knowing:\r\n\r\n- **Allowlisting is on the numeric user id, never the login.** A login can\r\n  be renamed and the freed name registered by somebody else. A login in\r\n  `config.yaml` raises at startup rather than never matching.\r\n- **The cold-start watermark is load-bearing.** The poller sees *open* PRs,\r\n  not `opened` events; without it the first poll would review the whole\r\n  backlog in one pass.\r\n\r\nEvery accept/reject decision is logged with its reason code.\r\n\r\n### Config loader \u2014 `src/pr_review_agent/config.py`\r\n\r\nStrict `config.yaml` loader. Unknown keys and malformed values raise\r\n`ConfigError` at startup; a typo in a safety setting must never fall back\r\nto a default that spends tokens. `config.example.yaml` is shipped and\r\ntested as loadable.\r\n\r\n### Poller \u2014 `src/pr_review_agent/poller/`\r\n\r\n- Three **repo-wide** endpoints per cycle (`/pulls?state=open`,\r\n  `/issues/comments`, `/pulls/comments`) \u2014 one request per endpoint\r\n  regardless of how many PRs are open, which is what keeps the rate-limit\r\n  arithmetic in #1 true.\r\n- **ETag conditional GETs.** A `304` costs nothing against the rate limit.\r\n- **Adaptive interval:** 10 s while active, \u00d72 decay per quiet cycle to a\r\n  600 s ceiling, snapping back to the floor on any `200`.\r\n- **Rate-limit handling:** bounded retries on `403`/`429` carrying\r\n  `Retry-After` (a plain `403` \u2014 bad token \u2014 is not retried), transport\r\n  errors wrapped in `GitHubClientError`, malformed headers tolerated, and\r\n  the interval forced to its ceiling when `x-ratelimit-remaining` reaches\r\n  the configured floor.\r\n\r\n### Dedupe keys\r\n\r\n    pr_opened:{repo}:{pr}:{head_sha}\r\n    mention:{repo}:{pr}:{comment_id}\r\n\r\nThe mention key excludes `head_sha` on purpose: the same comment must never\r\ntrigger twice, and a later push must not revive it.\r\n\r\n## Not in this PR\r\n\r\nDeliberately deferred, in dependency order:\r\n\r\n- Mapping poll payloads to `PullRequest` / `Comment` and feeding the\r\n  classifier; the loop that calls `poll_once()` on a schedule\r\n- Queue and per-PR lease (SQLite)\r\n- Budget governor \u2014 **lands before the review worker**\r\n- `ReviewEngine` adapter, publisher, retention sweep\r\n- GitHub token plumbing and the reviewer account id\r\n\r\n## Follow-ups\r\n\r\n- #3 \u2014 persist the watermark and ETag cache; decide how `/issues/comments`\r\n  payloads map to a PR (`head_sha`, `pr_number`, plain-issue filter, draft\r\n  vs. mention); migrate `GitHubClient` to async.\r\n- #4 \u2014 PR-Agent as a second `ReviewEngine` (`pr_agent_litellm`), API-key\r\n  mode only.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n    python -m pytest -q          # 122 passed, no network, no tokens\r\n    python -m ruff check .       # clean\r\n    python -m ruff format --check .\r\n\r\nThe trigger pipeline is pure functions over fixtures; the poller tests use\r\n`httpx.MockTransport`.\r\n\r\nRefs #1",
